<div class='page-hero'><div><h1 class='hero-title'>10 · THROUGH — 穿过三维通道、熬过难关与彻底审阅<span class='hero-badge'>📖 EPE Ch.2 §6 & Ch.9 §6</span></h1><p class='hero-sub'>THROUGH: Tunnel Penetration, Endurance, Completion & Insight</p></div><div style='font-size:0.88em;color:#475569;font-weight:600;'>共 <b>47</b> 个独立义项 • <b>141</b> 句中英对照例句</div></div>
<details class='epe-book-drawer' open><summary class='epe-drawer-bar'><span>📚 《English Prepositions Explained》(Seth Lindstromberg) 原著核心精讲 — Chapter 1 (§17) & Chapter 2 (§6 THROUGH) & Chapter 9 (§6 THROUGH vs ACROSS vs OVER, §8.2)</span><span style='font-size:0.84em;color:#6366f1;font-weight:600;'>点击收起 / 展开原书理论图式 ▾</span></summary><div class='epe-drawer-grid'><div class='epe-box-card'><div class='epe-box-title'>🧭 原著空间与功能核心图式 (Core Schema)</div><div><b>三维通道穿透 (Into, then out the other end) 与「经验实体化 (Reification)」</b>：主体从三维媒介或通道的一端进入，穿过内部，从另一端走出。在短语动词中，它既是核心完结体小品词（<i>think it through</i> 比 <i>think about</i> 更透彻），也是表达“熬过艰难经历”的首选词。</div><div class='epe-box-title' style='margin-top:12px;'>📝 原书典型语料例句 (Authentic Examples from EPE)</div><div class='epe-quote-chip'>📌 <i>My parents went through a bitter divorce when I was a child. / He says he's been through hell.</i> (将苦难经历实体化为必须穿越的隧道) [Ch.2 (23), (25)]</div><div class='epe-quote-chip'>📌 <i>It's not too late to change your mind, you don't have to go through with this.</i> [Ch.9 (56)]</div></div><div class='epe-box-card'><div class='epe-box-title'>⚖️ 原书近义小品词深度辨析与隐喻机制 (Key Contrasts & Metaphors)</div><ul class='epe-contrast-list'><li><b>THROUGH vs ACROSS vs OVER (Ch.9 §6.1.2 Fig.9.20 经典过河对比)</b>：<i>walk through a stream</i>（趟水穿过，脚会湿，处于水介质内部） vs <i>walk across a stream</i>（踩石头或冰面从平面横渡，脚不湿） vs <i>walk over a stream</i>（从拱桥上越过）。</li><li><b>THROUGH vs THROUGHOUT (Ch.9 §8.2.4)</b>：THROUGH 强调<b>动态推进并成功走出出口</b>（故说 <i>Help me make it through the night</i> 绝不能用 *throughout）；THROUGHOUT 则静态强调充满整个时间或三维空间的每一处角落。</li></ul></div></div></details>

